   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Truckin'** (1 other source): A monitor check leads into the opening Truckin' [1]\n- **Brown Eyed Women** (1 review): Jerry gets the first verse wrong [2]\n- **Tennessee Jed** (1 review): Described as solid [8]\n- **Black Peter** (1 review): Listener calls it their favorite Black Peter ever, with a gentle feel [8]\n- **Casey Jones** (1 review): Called one of the best versions of this song [3]\n- **One More Saturday Night** (1 review): Played fast and rocking, with prominent Phil and no Donna Jean [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Mister Charlie**: rare: 13 archived performances [14]\n- **Run Rudolph Run**: rare: 7 archived performances [14]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd71-12-09.sbd.kaplan.3345.sbeok.shnf** (recommended): soundboard; 21 songs; 125 min; rated 4.42/5 by 12 [1]. Said about its sound: Quality is good overall, with a bit of hiss typical of these shows; The piano distorts during this song; Instruments and vocals sound crisp and clean, more so than many shows from this era [2][3][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The recording preserves stage banter, which makes the listener feel present [6]\n- A distinctive period with both Keith and Pigpen in the band [9]\n- The next night has more downloads and reviews, but this show is also very good [4]\n- Better than the previous three months because Ron is back in the band [7]\n- Better than the following months because Donna Jean has not yet joined [7]\n- The first set on 12/10 is far stronger than this show; the band may have been tired from the Felt Forum shows [8]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd71-12-09.sbd.kaplan.3345.sbeok.shnf**: source: Soundboard [1]. Also: Taped as MSR with Latvala C mics, then transferred to DAT and CDR; Seth Kaplan converted it with EAC to SHN; Darrin Sacks uploaded it [1]",
